# x86_64 baseline, refreshed at the end of the hardening branch.
# Measured locally with scripts/check-sizes.sh on the reference desktop
# at commit c84f4ad, rustc 1.98.1 from rust-toolchain.toml, release
# profile (fat LTO, codegen-units=1, panic=abort, strip). The same sizes
# came out of a build in the repository and of one from a `git archive`
# of c84f4ad in another directory. This is NOT the size of the current
# branch tip: later commits changed code (a symlink message in the
# state-folder code), and the baseline is refreshed again from the
# final commit. The per-area account of the growth over the previous
# baseline (inacircle 900352 671864, Plan 7) is in
# docs/benchmarks/binary-size.md. The native CI runner builds the same
# c84f4ad to inacircle 1082248 / 822040 and inacircle-text 695048 /
# 397298 (CI run 40835264396), a few bytes apart (cause not analysed).
inacircle 1082216 822056
inacircle-text 695000 397314
